Package: MedPower
Title: Power and Sample Size for Mediation Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Tatsuro", "Ozaki", email = "t.ozaki@keio.jp",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Calculates approximate power and sample size for joint
    significance tests of natural indirect effects in mediation models with
    binary exposure and continuous or binary mediators and outcomes.
    Supports exposure-mediator interaction and user-specified variance
    inflation factors (VIFs) for covariate adjustment. With compatible
    design inputs and residual variances, VIF corrections to coefficient
    variances are exact under correctly specified homoskedastic linear
    models and approximate for logistic models. The continuous-mediator,
    binary-outcome calculation uses a rare-outcome approximation. The
    retained power approximation requires positive exposure-to-mediator
    and exposed-group mediator-to-outcome coefficients.
